%I A401684 #19 Nov 13 2026 17:37:57
%S A401684 14,50,86,122,158,194,230,266,302,338,374,410,446,482,518,554,590,626,
%T A401684 662,698,734,770,806,842,878,914,950,986,1022,1058,1094,1130,1166,
%U A401684 1202,1238,1274,1310,1346,1382,1418,1454,1490,1526,1562,1598,1634,1670,1706,1742,1778
%N A401684 Number of lattice points on the complete edge skeleton of a stella octangula.
%C A401684 Here n is the number of equal segments along each short edge of the framework, so each of its 36 edges contains n+1 lattice points, including endpoints. The corresponding solid stella octangula contains A007588(n+1) lattice points.
%C A401684 A stella octangula consists of two interpenetrating regular tetrahedra. Its complete edge skeleton comprises the 24 edges connecting the eight outer vertices to the six vertices of the central octahedron, together with the 12 edges of that octahedron, giving 36 edges and 14 vertices in total. These may be called the skeleton stella octangula numbers.
%C A401684 Each of the 36 edges contributes n-1 interior lattice points. Counting the 14 vertices only once therefore gives
%C A401684 a(n) = 14 + 36*(n-1).
%C A401684 Equivalently, a(n) counts the lattice points on the complete edge skeleton, excluding points strictly interior to the triangular faces or the solid.
%C A401684 For comparison, A142241 counts the lattice points on the 12 edges of the two interpenetrating tetrahedra (including their six shared vertices), while excluding the interior points of the central octahedron's 12 edges. The present sequence includes those additional points, giving
%C A401684 a(n) = A142241(n-1) + 12*(n-1), n >= 1.
%H A401684 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A401684/b401684.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A401684 <a href="/index/Rec#order_02">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (2,-1).
%F A401684 a(n) = 36*n - 22.
%F A401684 G.f.: 2*x*(7 + 11*x)/(1-x)^2.
%e A401684 For n = 3, the two tetrahedral frames contain 62 distinct lattice points (A142241(2)). Adding the 12 central octahedral edges contributes 12*(3-1) = 24 further points, giving a(3) = 86. The corresponding complete outer surface contains 110 lattice points (A005914(3)), while the solid contains 124 lattice points (A007588(4)).
%t A401684 36*Range[50] - 22 (* _Paolo Xausa_, Nov 13 2026 *)
%Y A401684 Cf. A005914, A007588, A142241.
%K A401684 nonn,easy,new
%O A401684 1,1
%A A401684 _Peter M. Chema_, Nov 02 2026
